1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,404
Two sugary drinks a day alone raised blood pressure risk 52 percent over 25 years - and soda's not the only culprit.

2
00:00:07,772 --> 00:00:10,123
Deli meat and alcohol play a role too.

3
00:00:10,491 --> 00:00:14,259
Six slices of deli turkey or ham pack half your daily sodium limit.

4
00:00:14,627 --> 00:00:19,432
Ask for freshly roasted chicken breast instead, or pick "low-sodium" if it's packaged.

5
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:22,034
Heavy drinking stiffens blood vessel walls.

6
00:00:22,402 --> 00:00:33,588
Moderating it dropped systolic pressure by 5.5 points in Mayo Clinic research - try hibiscus tea instead, shown in a Tufts study to cut it by about 7 points in six weeks.

7
00:00:33,956 --> 00:00:37,884
And soda's sugar spikes insulin, making your body hold extra sodium.

8
00:00:38,252 --> 00:00:42,735
Swap it for sparkling water instead - same fizz, none of the sugar.
